WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.167 --> 00:00:02.902
Jesse, in the
past seven battles,

00:00:02.968 --> 00:00:04.570
you have been faced
with fierce competitors

00:00:04.637 --> 00:00:06.840
and you've knocked them all
out of this competition.

00:00:06.906 --> 00:00:08.974
And if you win today,
will match the most

00:00:09.041 --> 00:00:11.110
amount of money ever
earned in "Forged in Fire"

00:00:11.210 --> 00:00:14.013 line:14%
history, $50,000.

00:00:14.080 --> 00:00:15.782
Your competitor
has two Gladiator

00:00:15.848 --> 00:00:16.816
of the Forge titles of his own.

00:00:16.883 --> 00:00:17.850
Oh.

00:00:17.950 --> 00:00:19.819
Jesse, in order
to win the day,

00:00:19.919 --> 00:00:21.921
you're going to have
to beat this guy--

00:00:21.988 --> 00:00:23.890
[dramatic music]

00:00:23.990 --> 00:00:25.958
GRADY POWELL: --Kurt.

00:00:26.025 --> 00:00:27.093
My name is Kurt.

00:00:27.193 --> 00:00:29.328
I'm a two-time
Gladiator of the Forge.

00:00:29.395 --> 00:00:31.464
Now I get another
chance at beating Jesse,

00:00:31.530 --> 00:00:32.965
and then he can feel
what it's like to have

00:00:33.065 --> 00:00:34.500
a loss under his belt.

00:00:34.567 --> 00:00:37.369
This battle will consist
of eight hours of forging

00:00:37.436 --> 00:00:39.972
competition where you will
build one of these three blades

00:00:40.039 --> 00:00:43.343
from our wall of
gladiator weapons.

00:00:43.409 --> 00:00:45.110
Today, you're going
to need to build this.

00:00:45.210 --> 00:00:47.414
JESSE (VOICEOVER): I
hope it's not a dolabra.

00:00:49.882 --> 00:00:51.184
GRADY POWELL: The dolabra.

00:00:54.754 --> 00:00:56.589
NARRATOR: The dolabra
was a versatile weapon

00:00:56.656 --> 00:01:00.193
used by the Roman Empire army
in the first century and beyond.

00:01:00.293 --> 00:01:03.062
Featuring a massive axe head
on one side and a sharp pick

00:01:03.162 --> 00:01:04.931
on the other, the
versatile battle axe

00:01:04.998 --> 00:01:06.832
doubled as a tool for
soldiers who would need

00:01:06.932 --> 00:01:09.235
to fell trees and clear brush.

00:01:09.335 --> 00:01:11.171
In the Colosseum,
the dolabra's ability

00:01:11.237 --> 00:01:14.040
to deliver deadly chops and
lethal blows against an enemy

00:01:14.107 --> 00:01:16.209
made it a favorite
weapon of the gladiators.

00:01:16.309 --> 00:01:17.843
Bladesmiths, this is it.

00:01:17.910 --> 00:01:20.413
This is the last battle in our
Colosseum-themed competition,

00:01:20.513 --> 00:01:23.015
Gladiator of the
Forge, so good luck.

00:01:23.115 --> 00:01:24.050
Your time starts now.

00:01:24.150 --> 00:01:25.685
[rock music]

00:01:25.752 --> 00:01:27.287
JESSE (VOICEOVER): My game plan
is to forge out this canister,

00:01:27.387 --> 00:01:29.422
cut the canister in half
for the outer jacket,

00:01:29.488 --> 00:01:32.157
and then forge out a 20-layer
random pattern billet,

00:01:32.224 --> 00:01:33.692
and have that as a sandwich.

00:01:33.759 --> 00:01:36.929
I'm setting up my San Mai so
that there's already a gap.

00:01:36.996 --> 00:01:39.399
After I get this
entire thing welded,

00:01:39.466 --> 00:01:42.268
then I'm prepared to begin
drawing out my blade.

00:01:42.368 --> 00:01:44.203
After I get the axe
head shaped out,

00:01:44.269 --> 00:01:45.437
it's time to go on to the pick.

00:01:45.504 --> 00:01:47.607
This is not your
traditional pickaxe.

00:01:47.674 --> 00:01:52.211
It's a recurved pick axe, so I
do that with my good old trusty

00:01:52.277 --> 00:01:53.813
hand hammer and the anvil horn.

00:01:53.880 --> 00:01:56.449
GRADY POWELL: Jesse's this
blade is looking badass.

00:01:56.516 --> 00:01:58.751
Now with the blade pretty
much forged to shape,

00:01:58.818 --> 00:02:01.020
it's time for the quench.

00:02:01.087 --> 00:02:02.288
GRADY POWELL: There
we go, all right.

00:02:02.354 --> 00:02:04.891
Jesse has his axe head quenched.

00:02:04.991 --> 00:02:08.261
He still has to
get that pick done.

00:02:08.361 --> 00:02:09.262
Boom.

00:02:09.329 --> 00:02:11.897
Jesse has a fully
quenched blade.

00:02:11.964 --> 00:02:13.198
It's great.

00:02:13.298 --> 00:02:15.902
It's a little bit heavy,
so I can definitely

00:02:16.002 --> 00:02:17.269
spend a lot of
time on the grinder

00:02:17.336 --> 00:02:21.273
and make sure it's as
light as it needs to be.

00:02:21.340 --> 00:02:23.609
One of the parameters
is a leather wrap,

00:02:23.676 --> 00:02:26.012
so it's time to
give it some flair.

00:02:26.112 --> 00:02:28.447
I want it to look
like a bloody mess.

00:02:28.548 --> 00:02:30.349
GRADY POWELL: What
is Jesse doing?

00:02:30.449 --> 00:02:32.885
He's trying to make it
look like it's bloodied up.

00:02:32.952 --> 00:02:34.620
GRADY POWELL: How long does
that stuff take to dry?

00:02:34.720 --> 00:02:38.624
Long enough that I'm
going to have red hands.

00:02:38.691 --> 00:02:42.895
This thing looks so menacing,
even my hands look bloody.

00:02:42.962 --> 00:02:45.365
Last thing I'm going to do
is put an edge on this thing.

00:02:45.431 --> 00:02:47.033
KURT: This time I
go with 16 layers

00:02:47.099 --> 00:02:51.304
because that's four less chances
of a forge weld not taking.

00:02:51.404 --> 00:02:53.306
If I cut it up four
times, I'll still

00:02:53.373 --> 00:02:58.377
have 64 layers total with that
1095 core for the same length.

00:02:58.444 --> 00:03:00.713
All the forge welds took, so
once I get the length that I

00:03:00.780 --> 00:03:02.614
need, I can cut it
up into four pieces,

00:03:02.715 --> 00:03:06.018
stack it, and draw it
out to get the 64 layers.

00:03:06.085 --> 00:03:08.287
Good.

00:03:08.387 --> 00:03:09.889
Now that I'm confident
that the welds are good,

00:03:09.956 --> 00:03:13.226
I can draw it out and then
forge weld the San Mai.

00:03:13.292 --> 00:03:16.128
I see that some of the
welds around the eye

00:03:16.195 --> 00:03:18.598
are splitting about
quarter of an inch.

00:03:18.665 --> 00:03:21.100
I drifted the eye
walls too thin,

00:03:21.167 --> 00:03:22.902
and there's a crack
going right down it.

00:03:22.969 --> 00:03:25.838 line:8%
I just want to do an edge
quench on the axe head

00:03:25.939 --> 00:03:28.540 line:8%
because if there
is too much stress

00:03:28.607 --> 00:03:30.944
on that cracked
weld around the eye,

00:03:31.010 --> 00:03:33.145
it could blow the
entire weld apart.

00:03:33.245 --> 00:03:35.481
I'm hoping that this
heat treat goes well.

00:03:39.719 --> 00:03:41.020
All right, guys.

00:03:41.120 --> 00:03:44.223
We've got two bladesmiths with
two fully quenched weapons.

00:03:44.289 --> 00:03:45.758
These guys are
seriously neck and neck.

00:03:45.825 --> 00:03:47.093
Yep.

00:03:47.160 --> 00:03:49.395
KURT: The last time that
I lost against Jesse, it

00:03:49.462 --> 00:03:50.662
was because of the handle.

00:03:50.729 --> 00:03:53.465
So I'm going a little
extra on this one.

00:03:53.565 --> 00:03:56.369
Kurt's been spending a lot
of time with that handle.

00:03:56.436 --> 00:03:59.171
Last challenge,
make it beautiful.

00:03:59.271 --> 00:04:01.406
I finally have
everything put together,

00:04:01.506 --> 00:04:03.676
and I am extremely happy now.

00:04:03.743 --> 00:04:06.879
Hopefully, my weapon is
good enough to beat Jesse.

00:04:06.979 --> 00:04:12.018
GRADY POWELL: 5, 4, 3, 2, 1.

00:04:12.118 --> 00:04:13.919
Bladesmiths, put
down your tools.

00:04:13.986 --> 00:04:15.154
This round is over.

00:04:15.221 --> 00:04:16.222
Good job.

00:04:16.322 --> 00:04:17.256
It was fun.

00:04:17.323 --> 00:04:18.858
I'm very impressed.

00:04:18.925 --> 00:04:22.729
Gladiators to the forge, Your
dolabras look evenly matched,

00:04:22.795 --> 00:04:24.697
but it's time to find out
what kind of lethal damage

00:04:24.764 --> 00:04:25.665
they will do.

00:04:25.765 --> 00:04:29.368
This is the kill test.

00:04:29.435 --> 00:04:31.270
Kurt, you're up first.

00:04:31.337 --> 00:04:32.505
You ready for this?
- I'm ready.

00:04:32.572 --> 00:04:33.706
All right, let's do this.

00:04:33.773 --> 00:04:37.410
[dramatic music]

00:05:03.536 --> 00:05:04.570
Damn.

00:05:11.977 --> 00:05:14.379
All right, Kurt, let's
talk about your dolabra here.

00:05:14.446 --> 00:05:17.450
First up, it is razor sharp.

00:05:17.550 --> 00:05:19.485
That dummy is going to have
a headache for a long time.

00:05:19.552 --> 00:05:21.387
Now, using this on
that ballistics dummy,

00:05:21.454 --> 00:05:22.921
it is amazing.

00:05:22.988 --> 00:05:26.859
Every thrust with your
pick, here, penetrated this

00:05:26.959 --> 00:05:30.262
because the balance you have
here allows for nice thrust

00:05:30.362 --> 00:05:31.697
and delivery on that.

00:05:31.798 --> 00:05:35.234
But during the test, you
lost a section right here.

00:05:35.334 --> 00:05:37.169
One of the layers
from your blade right

00:05:37.236 --> 00:05:38.904
here didn't weld
all the way through.

00:05:38.971 --> 00:05:42.108
But looking at this,
your core is still solid.

00:05:42.174 --> 00:05:45.244
So it's still going to be a
functional and testable blade.

00:05:45.344 --> 00:05:50.049
And overall, sir, your
dolabra will kill.

00:05:50.116 --> 00:05:51.450
Thank you, Doug.

00:05:51.550 --> 00:05:53.586
Jesse, you ready?

00:05:53.653 --> 00:05:55.254
All right, let's do this.

00:05:55.321 --> 00:05:58.858
[dramatic music]

00:06:28.220 --> 00:06:29.321
All right, Jesse.

00:06:29.388 --> 00:06:30.556
Let's talk about
your dolabra here.

00:06:30.656 --> 00:06:32.992
First up, you have a
heavier blade here,

00:06:33.059 --> 00:06:36.628
but it serves it very well when
you're doing damage like that.

00:06:36.695 --> 00:06:39.265
The feel of the weapon
really allows it to go deep

00:06:39.365 --> 00:06:41.300
into this ballistics dummy.

00:06:41.367 --> 00:06:45.104
Overall, sir, your
dolabra, it will kill.

00:06:45.204 --> 00:06:46.105
Thank you.

00:06:46.172 --> 00:06:48.340
[dramatic music]

00:06:48.440 --> 00:06:49.408
All right, gentlemen.

00:06:49.508 --> 00:06:50.776
You know what time it is.

00:06:50.877 --> 00:06:52.912
It's time for our strength
test, the Roman armor

00:06:52.979 --> 00:06:55.047
and shield chop.

00:06:55.147 --> 00:06:56.348
And Kurt, you are up first.

00:06:56.415 --> 00:06:57.516
Oh, destroy it.

00:06:57.583 --> 00:06:59.217
[laughs] I can't wait to.

00:06:59.318 --> 00:07:02.889
[dramatic music]

00:07:29.348 --> 00:07:30.550
That was pretty cool.

00:07:33.786 --> 00:07:36.255
So Kurt, this is a
good-looking weapon.

00:07:36.355 --> 00:07:37.957
The leather wrap you
did and the texturing

00:07:38.057 --> 00:07:41.594
up on the handle actually make
it quite comfortable to swing.

00:07:41.661 --> 00:07:43.228
The issue I have is
this delamination.

00:07:43.295 --> 00:07:44.196
[clank]

00:07:44.296 --> 00:07:45.765
It's come further open.

00:07:45.865 --> 00:07:47.800
It didn't affect
using it at all,

00:07:47.866 --> 00:07:52.604
but I do worry that that's going
to continue to be a problem.

00:07:52.671 --> 00:07:54.239
All right, Jesse.
You're up.

00:07:54.306 --> 00:07:55.608
You ready?

00:07:55.708 --> 00:07:56.609
Sure.

00:07:56.709 --> 00:07:58.277
[laughs]

00:07:58.344 --> 00:08:01.881
[dramatic music]

00:08:18.597 --> 00:08:20.566
[forceful exhale]

00:08:20.666 --> 00:08:23.101
All right, Jesse, right
off the bat, great look.

00:08:23.201 --> 00:08:24.203
It's a good shape.

00:08:24.270 --> 00:08:25.838
The pattern came
out really nice.

00:08:25.905 --> 00:08:28.307
And where it really stands out
is right there on the socket,

00:08:28.374 --> 00:08:29.308
which is kind of cool.

00:08:29.375 --> 00:08:30.609
You still got an edge.

00:08:30.675 --> 00:08:31.644
Everything's right and tight.

00:08:31.711 --> 00:08:32.845
Everything's solid.

00:08:32.945 --> 00:08:34.814
All in all, it held
up beautifully.

00:08:34.914 --> 00:08:35.815
Great job.

00:08:35.915 --> 00:08:38.450
Thank you.

00:08:38.550 --> 00:08:40.519
You had fun, didn't you?

00:08:40.586 --> 00:08:42.421
Well, Jesse, Kurt, I
couldn't have asked

00:08:42.488 --> 00:08:44.723
for a better final match-up.

00:08:44.823 --> 00:08:46.292
But at the end of the
day, only one of you

00:08:46.392 --> 00:08:49.562
can take home that final title
and the last check for $5,000.

00:08:49.628 --> 00:08:51.096
The Gladiator of the Forge is--

00:08:51.163 --> 00:08:54.300
[dramatic music]

00:08:57.436 --> 00:08:58.337
--Jesse.

00:08:58.404 --> 00:09:00.506
You are unstoppable.

00:09:00.573 --> 00:09:01.907
Now, Kurt, you should
be proud of your work,

00:09:02.007 --> 00:09:03.809
but unfortunately, your
dolabra did not make the cut.

00:09:03.909 --> 00:09:05.478
I'm going to have
to ask you to please

00:09:05.545 --> 00:09:06.512
step off the forge floor.
- Thank you, gentlemen.

00:09:06.578 --> 00:09:07.479
GRADY POWELL: Thank you, Kurt.

00:09:07.546 --> 00:09:08.480
Jesse, congrats, man.

00:09:08.581 --> 00:09:09.515
You deserve it.

00:09:09.582 --> 00:09:10.849
Thank you.

00:09:10.916 --> 00:09:13.185
So Jesse took another title.

00:09:13.252 --> 00:09:15.121
And I don't disagree at all.

00:09:15.187 --> 00:09:17.856
He once again turned
in an awesome weapon.

00:09:17.956 --> 00:09:19.491
Kurt, you did a good job, man.

00:09:19.592 --> 00:09:20.459
KURT: Thank you.

00:09:20.526 --> 00:09:21.894
Chin high.

00:09:21.961 --> 00:09:24.329
Well, Jesse, I've got
one word to describe you,

00:09:24.396 --> 00:09:25.797
and that is "impressive."

00:09:25.897 --> 00:09:28.900 line:8%
You just won your eighth
Gladiator of the Forge title,

00:09:29.000 --> 00:09:31.503 line:8%
and you have $50,000
to take home with you.

00:09:31.570 --> 00:09:32.471 line:14%
Congratulations.

00:09:32.538 --> 00:09:33.472 line:14%
[applause]

00:09:33.539 --> 00:09:34.907
Thank you.

00:09:35.007 --> 00:09:37.576
This experience was
definitely once in a lifetime

00:09:37.676 --> 00:09:39.111
I just won 50 grand.

00:09:39.211 --> 00:09:42.815
I'm planning on putting so
much of it into bladesmithing.

00:09:42.915 --> 00:09:45.884
I already made a spreadsheet of
all the tools I'm going to buy.

00:09:45.984 --> 00:09:48.353
I'll finally live
the dream, as opposed

00:09:48.420 --> 00:09:49.955
to just dreaming the dream.

00:09:50.022 --> 00:09:53.125
[music playing]

